From 24f3878ae99afa7814c49b6c634f5e6e3b01ee8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:17:28 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 10/29] usb: tegra124: force VBUS and trace the device-mode
 bring-up

- tegra124-udc now uses CI_HDRC_DUAL_ROLE_NOT_OTG plus
  CI_HDRC_FORCE_VBUS_ACTIVE_ALWAYS: VBUS lives in the palmas PMIC, not
  the controller's OTGSC register, so the OTG path never saw a session
- re-add the palmas and gpio extcons to usb@7d000000 with dr_mode
  peripheral; both now resolve after the palmas MFD fix
- add n9trace breadcrumbs in PMC scratch registers, a 8s hang timer and
  an n9.reader pass that prints them; a userspace trigger (n9.trigger)
  defers the probe so the log can be captured while it runs
- step prints in the glue, phy and UDC paths; raw PORT_CAP poke in
  ci_udc_pullup shows the padctl never set up the port
- remains diagnostic: the controller reaches device mode and sets the
  pull-up, but the host still sees no device

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code with DeepSeek Flash v4.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
